Paint the Windows window edge instead of black

Purpose: on Windows the main window shows a ~3 px black frame.
Upstream forces DirectComposition (GDK_DEBUG=dcomp), which draws the
transparent area around a CSD window black; style-win.css hides it
with margin: -9px, but GTK keeps a 12 px resize area, so 3 px stay.

Approach: keep the -9 px and paint the leftover 3 px with a solid
spread shadow in the border colour. Removing it (margin: -12px) kills
the black, but also resizing from the right and bottom edges.

Constraints: Windows only (style-win.css). Upstream candidate.
